  [
   "Complaint trend (Kemi Adeyemi)",
   "Late delivery complaints were 31% of tickets in October, up from 22% in September. Most come from Abuja and Port Harcourt orders."
  ],
  [
   "Option comparison (Tunde Bello)",
   "Eko Express ₦7.44m a month, SwiftLane ₦9.38m. Abuja and Port Harcourt delivery: Eko 3 to 5 days, SwiftLane 1 to 3 days. Tunde recommended Eko Express. Ifeoma said \"sounds good\" at 10:12."
  ],
  [
   "Budget check (Amaka Obi, 10:18)",
   "The Q1 courier line is ₦8.5m a month. Eko Express fits. SwiftLane would need CEO approval."
  ],
  [
   "Delivery times",
   "Eko Express has told Tunde informally it can deliver to Abuja and Port Harcourt in four days. There is no written confirmation."
  ],
  [
   "10:18",
   "Kemi asked to switch the packaging supplier. There is no paper. Ifeoma deferred it."
  ],
  [
   "10:26",
   "Ifeoma decided: Eko Express from 4 January 2027, as long as Eko confirms Abuja and Port Harcourt delivery in writing."
  ],
  [
   "Actions",
   "Tunde, written confirmation from Eko Express by Tuesday 1 December. Amaka, budget line in writing to Ifeoma by Monday 30 November. Kemi, packaging supplier paper to Ifeoma by Wednesday 2 December."
  ],
  [
   "Next meeting",
   "Thursday 3 December 2026, 10:00 WAT."
  ]
